{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Apex",
  "theme": "apex",
  "_about": "AAR's own sport dash, generated by tools/gen_apex.py (edit that and regenerate): speed (SPEED_SCALE) and revs (0..8) as two upright light columns at the far left and right, lit in LED steps in the drive mode's colour (theme 'apex' modes), the speed and gear in big figures inside them, boost and oil on the left, coolant and fuel on the right, and a car seen from above in the middle with each tyre's pressure and temperature (a wheel turns amber under 1.9 bar). While the Waze map shows inside the theme ('mapUp') the middle is cut see-through and the tyre readouts step aside. Everything that isn't text is one shader (adash). The bottom row has the clock, range and outside temperature, BMW's gear letter left uncovered. Widget reference: shared/hud.js header.",
